## MIXED EXERCISE PAGE — REQUIRED INTERACTIVITY
This is one physical textbook page containing several different exercise mechanics. Keep exactly one outer section, but render every top-level activity as a semantic subgroup with `data-activity-kind` equal to its specific known section type (`activity_multiple_choice`, `activity_true_false`, `activity_fill_in_the_blank`, or `activity_open_ended_answer`). Do not turn any exercise into static text.

- Multiple choice: one `<fieldset>` per question, with the exact question in `<legend>`. Wrap every option in `<label class="activity-option">` containing `<input type="radio">`. Options in one question share a unique `name`; different questions use different names. Every option has a globally unique `data-activity-item="item-N"`, a visible focus style, and an accessible name from its label.
- True/false: one `<fieldset>` per statement and the statement in `<legend>`. Provide exactly two labelled radios with values `true` and `false`; the pair shares its own `name` and `data-activity-item`. Every button MUST visibly spell out the localized words `TRUE` and `FALSE` (or the source's exact Yes/No wording) using generated `activity_gen_*` text IDs when necessary. Never show only initials, icons, empty badges, CSS pseudo-content, or screen-reader-only words. Include `<span class="validation-mark hidden"></span>` in each option label.
- Written answers: pair every question and its own `<input type="text">` or `<textarea>` in one `data-question-response="item-N"` wrapper. The field immediately follows the question, is full-width below it, has a unique `data-activity-item`, unique `data-aria-id`, `tabindex="0"`, and `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Use a textarea for explanation/paragraph answers.
- Number `item-N` identifiers sequentially across the whole page. Never reuse an identifier between mechanics (except the intentional two-radio pair of one true/false statement).
- Preserve section headings and continuation content in source reading order. A question that continues from the previous printed page must remain visible and operable here; do not invent a missing stem.
- Native controls must remain keyboard operable and visibly focusable. Do not use custom click-only divs, scripts, or pointer-only interactions.
